[[2047,96,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The two-way switch controlling mirrors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               operates\nelectrical motors located in the right and left electrically-operated\ndoor mirrors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P61</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              respectively.</p><p>The switch is supplied when the ignition\nis switched on (INT/A) at pin 7 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , by the line for fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F6</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ;  Pin 1 is earthed.</p><p>Operating the switch in one direction or\nthe other, sends one of the two motors a positive and an earth signal,\nthereby determining the direction of rotation. The motors which\nadjust the vertical position are connected to pin 5 of the mirrors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P61</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , the motors which adjust the horizontal position are\nconnected to pin 3. According to the selector position, either the\nleft motors (output signals from pins 4 and 9 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ) or\nthe right motors (output signals from pins 12 and 2 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              )\nare connected;  the common supply comes out of pin 8 and is connected\nto pin 5 of the motors.</p><p>The switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is lit up when the\nside lights are switched on by means of the line coming from the\nstalk unit switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (pin 5).</p>"]]